# Adding a System Call to xv6

Man, the look on my face after running this for the first time:

```bash
cd xv6
ls
```

Kind of like when you’re running and your right side starts hurting.

Man, I can’t stand that :)

But after some time—and, admittedly, too many ChatGPT prompts of
“explain this now,” followed by even more questions arising from the
inevitable wall of endless text—I think I might have an idea what
some of these files do.

My biggest realization? **Operating systems are pretty damn fun.**

So fun that I made a video about adding a system call to xv6 :)

**[Watch the walkthrough →](YOUR_YOUTUBE_VIDEO_URL)**

And here’s a flowchart if you don’t want to hear me yapping :)

